window.products.push({"id":139632,"name":"WR51X10055 GE Refrigerator Defrost Heater Replacement Assembly Kit Kenmore Part Number GSH25JSXNSS TFX25PPBGWW GSH25ISXBSS GSHS6HGDBCSS GSH25JSDBSS GS","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":14.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/618jgAhjAmL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Ge Wr51x10055 Refrigerator Defrost Heater - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers AP3183311, 914088, AH303781, EA303781, PS303781, WR51X10030. Wr51x10055 Refrigerator Defrost Heater is compatible with General Electric and Hotpoint appliances. Ge Defrost Heater Wr51x10055 is a long, thin, and curved heating element that is typically located behind the back panel of the freezer compartment. The Defrost Heater Wr51x10055 fits hundreds of models and can be installed in a few minutes. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the Defrost Heater Assembly Wr51x10055? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Wr51x10055 Defrost Heater will help if your appliance is too warm, freezer is not defrosting, or there's a frost buildup. It is important to note that the wattage of the Part Number Wr51x10055 can vary depending on the specific model of the refrigerator. 💡 The Wr51x10055 Refrigerator Defrost Heater Kit is designed to melt any ice or frost that has built up on the evaporator coil of the refrigerator. The Refrigerator Defrost Heater Assembly Wr51x10055 is a crucial component of the refrigerator's defrost system, which helps to keep the unit running efficiently and prevent damage to the compressor. Our Part Wr51x10055 meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 How do I test my refrigerator defrost heater? First, unplug the refrigerator and locate the defrost heater, which is often behind the back panel of the freezer compartment. Locate defrost heater by unplugging fridge and checking behind freezer compartment panel. Remove the wires connected to the heater and set the multimeter to resistance mode. Place the probes on the terminals of the heater and check the reading against the recommended value in the manual. 💡 Where is the defrost heater located on a GE refrigerator? The defrost heater in a GE refrigerator is usually located behind the back panel of the freezer compartment. To access it, you may need to remove the panel by unscrewing the screws or pulling out the retaining clips. In some models, the defrost heater may be located on the bottom of the freezer compartment. The exact location of the defrost heater can vary depending on the specific model of the refrigerator.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/618jgAhjAmL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07MWPW6K2","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-139632","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07MWPW6K2","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07MWPW6K2","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
